  "notes": {
    "colon": "the chat-wrapped prompt ends 'ASSISTANT:', so the colon token immediately before the answer is the LAST PROMPT position; with KV caching its prefill record is step_records[0] (x14's handoff convention) and generated.scores[0] is the model's next-token distribution there",
    "candidates": "candidates are the vendored per-category lists, truncated to --n-candidates (the paper's 10); a candidate's readout token is its leading-space form's LAST token id (x13's 'token strings keep the caption's leading space' + the edit path's _token_id convention), the token that would be emitted at that position",
    "rank_rule": "1-based rank, ties count as better ranks (s2_eval._rank_of_row semantics)",
    "swap": "the paper's coordinate swap: V=[v_s v_t] with v = rows of W_U @ J_l (the raw J-lens vectors), c = pinv(V) @ h, h' = h + V @ (sigma(c) - c), sigma swapping the two coordinates; applied at ALL token positions of ALL workspace-band layers simultaneously (prefill rows AND every decode step) by reusing interventions.apply_edit's 'swap' mode per band layer",
    "source": "the source s is the model's spontaneously chosen item = its FIRST GENERATED TOKEN (the answer word's first emitted subword); its id cannot round-trip through the tokenizer as a string, so vectors are resolved by token id in this script (vectors_for_ids = interventions.lens_vectors' exact math keyed by id)",
    "target_selection": "targets are same-category candidates whose surface is not the model's answer and whose token is not among the model's top-10 next-token outputs at the colon (top-10 ids or their decoded surfaces), first --n-swaps in vendored order",
    "success": "success = the first generated word equals the target (case-insensitive; multiword targets count when the completion starts with them); target_in_top5 = the target's first subword id ranks <= 5 (RANK_RULE) in the swapped run's step-0 distribution",
    "decomposition_arm": "protocol part (c), the J-space vs non-J-space decomposition arm (k=16), is SKIPPED: the vendored jlens exposes no sparse nonnegative gradient-pursuit decomposition (jlens/lens.py provides transport/apply only) - recorded as a deviation"
  },
